{"cuisine/cuisine-of-saint-helena":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-saint-helena","n":"Saint Helenian cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Saint Helena","intro":[["The island of Saint Helena has been influenced by several European powers, by the inhabitants, (especially  enslaved people) and the ships passing through, during its history. This has affected the cuisine of Saint Helena, which now has a vibrant and international cuisine variety."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-saint-helena"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_Saint_Helena"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"The Saint Cooks","ref":"site/saintcooks-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"saintcooks.com","note":"St Helena island recipes such as plo and fishcakes from Robin and Emma-Jane, who are writing a St Helena cookbook.","url":"https://www.saintcooks.com/recipe/","suggested":true}]}],"cont":"African cuisine"},"cuisine/cuisine-of-atlanta":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-atlanta","n":"Cuisine of Atlanta","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southern-united-states"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["The cuisine of Atlanta reflects both Southern and much broader influences. The city is home to a mix of high-end chef-driven restaurants receiving praise at the national level, an ethnic restaurant scene along Buford Highway, and traditional Southern eateries."],["Atlanta is the birthplace of Coca-Cola. The fast food chain Chick-fil-A originated in  Hapeville, a suburb of Atlanta."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-atlanta"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_Atlanta"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuis