,"n":"Lorne sausage","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Scottish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Lorne sausage, also known as square sausage or slice sausage, is a traditional Scottish food item made from minced meat, rusk and spices. Although termed a sausage, no casing is used to hold the meat in shape, hence it is usually served as square slices from a formed block. It is a common component of the traditional Scottish breakfast."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-lorne-sausage"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorne_sausage"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Zwieback","ingredient/zwieback"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scottish Scran","ref":"site/scottishscran-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scottishscran.com","note":"Blog working through traditional Scottish dishes one recipe at a time.","url":"https://scottishscran.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Something Sweet Something Savoury: Scottish recipes","ref":"site/somethingsweetsomethingsavoury-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com","note":"Scottish home baking and cooking section of a UK food blog.","url":"https://somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com/category/scottish-recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Scottish cuisine","links":[["Clootie dumpling","dish/clootie-dumpling"],["Cock-a-leekie","dish/cock-a-leekie"],["Finnan haddie","dish/finnan-haddie"],["Haggis","dish/haggis"],["Haggis pakora","dish/haggis-pakora"],["Hobnob biscuit","dish/hobnob-biscuit"],["Mince and tatties","dish/mince-and-tatties"],["Rumbledethumps","dish/rumbledethumps"],["Scotch broth","dish/scotch-broth"],["Skirlie","dish/skirlie"],["Stornoway black pudding","dish/stornoway-black-pudding"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/45/Cooked_Scottish_square_sausage.jpg/500px-Cooked_Scottish_square_sausage.jpg","w":500,"h":703,"by":"AllyD","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cooked_Scottish_square_sausage.jpg"}},"ingredient/smen":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/smen","n":"Smen","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Smen is a salted, fermented butter native to North African cuisine (Algerian, Moroccan and Tunisian), as well as a traditional Yemeni dish. In countries like Jordan and Lebanon, samneh is a type of butter similar to clarified butter, while north African smen is a type of fermented butter similar to ghee."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-smen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Algerian cuisine","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",[["Mbesses","dish/mbesses"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Semolina","ingredient/semolina"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8e/Smen_msemmen.jpg/500px-Smen_msemmen.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"Lucyin","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smen_msemmen.jpg"}},"ingredient/toffee":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/toffee","n":"Toffee","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Toffee is an English confection made by caramelizing sugar or molasses (creating inverted sugar) along with butter, and occasionally flour. The mixture is heated until its temperature reaches the hard crack stage of 149 to 154 °C (300 to 310 °F). While being prepared, toffee is sometimes mixed with nuts or raisins."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-toffee"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.or